      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LONDON ROSE (6) returned from a four-month spell and was having her first run for the O'Connor stable when a dominant all-the-way winner last start over this distance at Northam. Has a new lease on life and can certainly take this next step. BONDITRAM (1) came from last in a small field to get up for third when resuming over this trip at Belmont last time out. Sure to prove tough to hold out in what looks an easier contest. LONDON'S RASCAL (4) is back from an 11-week spell. Finished just 3.5 lengths away in an $80k race at Belmont at the start of last prep. Can play a role with a similar effort today. FIREY PANZ (7) has won just one race in 65 and it came over three-and-a-half years ago. Hasn't been far away of late. One for the exotics. ARTIE'S ECLIPSE (3) won here maiden here at this distance two back. In the mix.",
